# tuning_data/ holds digests of tuning + calibration runs: small JSON
# summaries, CSV timeseries, diagnostic PNG plots, YAML config/summary
# snapshots, and a few keyframe JPEGs. Written by analyze_level_bag.py,
# the digest_*_bag.py scripts, and the focus/exposure calibration tools
# (focus_exposure_baseline.py, focus_sweep.py, …).
#
# Block everything by default, then re-allow only the small artifact
# types we expect. This makes it impossible to accidentally commit a raw
# rosbag2 SQLite/MCAP into the repo, no matter what someone runs.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!*.json
!*.csv
!*.png
# YAML config/summary snapshots + keyframe images from the focus/exposure
# calibration + baseline tools (baseline.yaml, summary.yaml, frame_*.jpg).
!*.yaml
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
# ...but NEVER the rosbag2 metadata sidecar — it pairs with the big .mcap
# we block (and the pi_deploy.sh deny-list excludes it too). Re-block it
# AFTER the !*.yaml allow so this line wins.
metadata.yaml
